{"resource":{"id":"rust-project-guide","title":"Rust — Project Guide","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Intermediate","readingTime":"17 min","pages":25,"lastUpdated":"June 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555949963-aa79dcee981c?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"End-to-end guide to shipping production Rust: planning, workspace design, testing, logging, APIs, databases, deployment, CI/CD, monitoring, docs, and maintenance."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Planning & Scoping"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Cargo Workspace Layout"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Architecture"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. API Development"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Database Integration"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Testing Strategy"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Logging & Observability"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. CI/CD & Deployment"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Monitoring & Maintenance"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Documentation"},{"id":"diagrams","label":"Architecture Diagrams"},{"id":"best","label":"Best Practices"},{"id":"mistakes","label":"Common Mistakes"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary & Key Takeaways"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust — Project Case Study","tag":"Programming","time":"27 min"},{"title":"Rust — Best Practices","tag":"Programming","time":"16 min"},{"title":"Rust — Advanced Concepts","tag":"Programming","time":"31 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Plan and structure a production Rust project.</li>\n          <li>Set up workspaces, testing, logging, and CI/CD.</li>\n          <li>Ship a Rust service with monitoring and docs.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Planning &amp; Scoping</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Start with a written charter: problem statement, non-goals, acceptance criteria, and risk register. Prefer a walking skeleton over an over-engineered design.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Tip</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Write the README before writing code.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Cargo Workspace Layout</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>novaledger/\n├── Cargo.toml       # [workspace]\n├── crates/\n│   ├── api/         # axum HTTP layer\n│   ├── domain/      # pure logic, no I/O\n│   ├── storage/     # sqlx repos\n│   └── worker/      # background jobs\n└── xtask/           # dev automation</code></pre></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Hexagonal workspace: domain at the core, adapters at the edge.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Architecture</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Layer traits for storage and clock; inject concrete implementations at the composition root. Keep domain crates <code>#![forbid(unsafe_code)]</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. API Development</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>use axum::{Router, routing::get, Json};\nasync fn health() -&gt; Json&lt;serde_json::Value&gt; {\n    Json(serde_json::json!({ &quot;ok&quot;: true }))\n}\npub fn app() -&gt; Router {\n    Router::new().route(&quot;/health&quot;, get(health))\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Database Integration</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Use <code>sqlx</code> with compile-time query checking, migrations under <code>migrations/</code>, and a repository trait per aggregate.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Testing Strategy</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Unit tests inline (<code>#[cfg(test)]</code> modules).</li>\n          <li>Integration tests under <code>tests/</code>.</li>\n          <li>Property tests via <code>proptest</code> for invariants.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Logging &amp; Observability</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Adopt <code>tracing</code> + <code>tracing-subscriber</code>. Emit JSON in production, human logs in dev. Wire OpenTelemetry for spans.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. CI/CD &amp; Deployment</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code># .github/workflows/ci.yml\n- run: cargo fmt --check\n- run: cargo clippy -- -D warnings\n- run: cargo test --workspace\n- run: cargo build --release</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Ship as a static musl binary or in a distroless container.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Monitoring &amp; Maintenance</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Expose <code>/metrics</code> (Prometheus), alert on error budget burn, and rotate dependencies weekly via <code>cargo update</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Documentation</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Publish rustdoc, keep an ADR log, and record runbooks for on-call.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"diagrams\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Architecture Diagrams</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>Client → API (axum) → Domain → Storage (Postgres)\n                             ↓\n                          Worker (queue)</code></pre></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Data flow from HTTP edge to persistence.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"best\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Best Practices</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>One binary crate per deployable.</li>\n          <li>Deny warnings and clippy lints in CI.</li>\n          <li>Prefer <code>thiserror</code> for libs, <code>anyhow</code> for bins.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mistakes\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Mixing async runtimes.</li>\n          <li>Blocking calls inside <code>#[tokio::main]</code>.</li>\n          <li>Unversioned migrations.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Structure first, features second. Deny warnings, embrace tracing, and automate the boring parts.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>axum or actix-web?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Both are excellent — axum has smoother ergonomics on modern Tokio.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Diesel or sqlx?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">sqlx for async + compile-time queries; Diesel for strict typed schemas.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Recommendations reflect current ecosystem norms as of 2026.</p>\n      </div></section>"}